            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\": \"Vulnerability, defenselessness, and total dependence on God, representing the marginalized who are objects of God's special protection and justice.\", \"primary_basis\": [\"Exodus 22:22-24\", \"Deuteronomy 10:18\", \"Psalm 68:5\", \"Isaiah 1:17\", \"James 1:27\"], \"alternatives\": [{\"meaning\": \"Israel or the Church in a state of desolation, mourning, or exile.\", \"basis\": [\"Lamentations 1:1\", \"Isaiah 54:4\"], \"prominence\": \"common\"}, {\"meaning\": \"Exemplary faith, devotion, and total surrender of resources to God.\", \"basis\": [\"1 Kings 17:8-16\", \"Mark 12:41-44\", \"Luke 2:36-38\"], \"prominence\": \"common\"}, {\"meaning\": \"Spiritual desolation or judgment, contrasted with a false sense of security (e.g., Babylon claiming not to be a widow).\", \"basis\": [\"Isaiah 47:8\", \"Revelation 18:7\"], \"prominence\": \"minority\"}], \"has_settled_consensus\": true, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"notes\": \"The widow is frequently grouped with the orphan and the alien in Scripture to form a triad representing the most vulnerable members of ancient society. Because they lacked a traditional male protector, they symbolically and practically represented those who must rely entirely on God, and for whom God demands strict social justice.\"}",
